# CFF citation metadata for the SIREN reference-class release.
# NOTE (TODO before Zenodo deposit): add ORCIDs if desired, and fill in `doi`
# once the deposit is minted from the GitHub tag v1.0.
# Validate with `cffconvert --validate` or https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or benchmark protocol, please cite both this
  software release and the accompanying preprint.
title: >-
  SIREN — a calibrated reference class for CRISPRi enhancer→gene prediction
  (code & results for "How far do simple baselines go in CRISPRi enhancer–gene
  prediction?")
authors:
  - given-names: Gabriele
    family-names: Bambini
    affiliation: "Università Commerciale Luigi Bocconi, Milano, Italia"
  - given-names: Lorenzo
    family-names: De Santis
    affiliation: "Università Commerciale Luigi Bocconi, Milano, Italia"
  - given-names: Andrea
    family-names: Tangherloni
    affiliation: "Università Commerciale Luigi Bocconi, Milano, Italia"
version: v1.0
date-released: "2026-08-23"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Gabriele-Bambini/siren-crispr-reference"
abstract: >-
  Leakage-safe benchmark study of CRISPRi enhancer→gene effect prediction on
  EPCrisprBenchmark K562 (10,356 valid pairs): a calibrated simple baseline
  (distance + cell-type-matched ATAC, gradient boosting + split-conformal
  intervals), the specificity wall for cross-cell-type and cross-screen
  transfer, a powered pre-registered negative on Enformer in-silico-silencing
  counterfactual deltas, baseline-adjusted sign-metric reporting, and an
  adversarial robustness program in which no variant beat the reference class.
keywords:
  - CRISPRi
  - enhancer-gene prediction
  - benchmark
  - conformal prediction
  - negative results
  - functional genomics
